commit 5513768e7d9919e8705bb3bcbf2ce366d6af8fea

C03: the screen-text final states its scope for see/identify/button requests, exposes no excerpt count, vetoes the echoed lens sentence and unwraps a fully quoted reply (SCREEN1809)

SCREEN1807 measured: «tomá un screenshot para ver la pantalla» and «identificá el botón» got no honest scope statement (only see/describe wordings asked for it) and copied the lens sentence «y cita cada una de esas líneas tal cual» as the reply; the English variant said «3 lines» from the exposed excerptLines and wrapped the whole reply in quotation marks. The composer now asks the scope statement for ver/identificar/botón wordings (naming buttons when a button was asked), projects only lineCount, phrases the lens so the lines follow the count, treats the lens sentence in a draft as a copied instruction, and strips one pair of quotation marks wrapping the whole reply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


